1
00:00:05,550 --> 00:00:10,120
Athena is the goddess of war and combat strategy, but also of the wisdom,

2
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:14,920
ability, sciences, and justice. She was one of the twelve principal deities that

3
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:20,710
lived at the Mount Olympus, and her name comes from the Greek term Ἀθῆναι that means "divine intelligence"

4
00:00:20,710 --> 00:00:23,730
or "ethical intelligence".

5
00:00:23,730 --> 00:00:29,279
There are several theories about her origin, the most extended says that her father was the same, Zeus.

6
00:00:29,279 --> 00:00:33,810
His first wife Metis, a Titaness, prophesied that their children would be

7
00:00:33,810 --> 00:00:39,460
more powerful than their own father. When she got pregnant he, scared, decided to swallow her.

8
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:44,780
Even though, she gave birth and Athena was born from Zeus' forehead with

9
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:49,220
Hephaestus' help, the god of fire and metals

10
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:52,680
who let her get out with his ax.

11
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:57,480
Others tell that she was Pallas' daughter, the titan of wisdom. When he tried to abuse her

12
00:00:57,489 --> 00:01:02,609
she killed him and the skin to make her a breastplate,

13
00:01:02,609 --> 00:01:09,640
the Égida and she put the wings in her feet. Even she was considered Poseidon's daughter,

14
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:15,510
god of seas, she got mad with him and she was adopted by Zeus.

15
00:01:15,510 --> 00:01:20,110
The unique thing that's clear is that her heart is closed for passions. She never had a husband or lover

16
00:01:20,110 --> 00:01:24,772
and she was known as "Athena the virgin" or Athena Parthenos, where the name

17
00:01:24,772 --> 00:01:30,770
of the most famous temple dedicated to her comes from, the Parthenon on the Acropolis.

18
00:01:30,770 --> 00:01:35,640
That's where it was a huge statue of her of 12 meters of height, built

19
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:41,920
by Fidias. Unlike other goddesses, she was represented always dressed,

20
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:44,990
with a long tunica and the Égida on her chest.

21
00:01:44,990 --> 00:01:49,090
Like the goddess of war and protector of heroes, she usually wears a helmet above

22
00:01:49,090 --> 00:01:54,610
the forehead to show her pacific face. In one hand she carries goldenrod, with which she gives

23
00:01:54,610 --> 00:01:59,920
protection to her favorites. And on the other hand she carries her shield with the head of the gorgon, Medusa,

24
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:05,850
gift of the hero Perseus for helped him to defeat her. She's usually accompanied by an owl,

25
00:02:05,850 --> 00:02:08,920
a bird that then became philosophy's symbol.

26
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:13,470
Other times, she carries a snake on her lap or her feet. It comes from the myth in which

27
00:02:13,470 --> 00:02:18,140
she became Erichthonius' adoptive mother and protector, the first king of Athens,

28
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:25,280
born of Hephaestus and Gaia. One day, she put him into a little basket and entrusted it to three of her sisters.

29
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:30,750
She didn't say what it had, but she warned them about don't open it until she came back. But couldn't

30
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:35,370
avoid it, and to their horror, they found the kid turned

31
00:02:35,370 --> 00:02:38,210
into a snake.

32
00:02:38,210 --> 00:02:42,930
When Erichthonius became the founder of Ancient Greece's capital,

33
00:02:42,930 --> 00:02:48,580
Athena competed with Poseidon to be the city's protector, still without a name. Poseidon

34
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:53,930
hit the ground with his trident, making appear a salty water fountain, and Athena

35
00:02:53,930 --> 00:02:59,230
planted an olive. Zeus decided that the tree had appeared first, choosing Athena

36
00:02:59,230 --> 00:03:03,490
as patron of the city, named in her honor.

37
00:03:03,490 --> 00:03:08,209
Another version tells that the Athenians voted to choose one of the gods. The women

38
00:03:08,209 --> 00:03:13,760
voted for Athena and the men for Poseidon. She won by only one vote,

39
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:18,470
and the god of the seas, angry, flooded the region. To calm his anger,

40
00:03:18,470 --> 00:03:21,970
women's right to vote was removed.

41
00:03:21,970 --> 00:03:26,560
Athena helped with the state's prosperity, encouraging the agriculture con the invention

42
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:31,319
of the plow and the rake. She also taught the men to tame the beasts and to produce fire.

43
00:03:31,319 --> 00:03:36,170
And not only, but they are also attributed to her several inventions related to science and art

44
00:03:36,170 --> 00:03:41,400
like the numbers, the navigation, the sewing, and even some instruments

45
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:44,190
like the flute or the trumpet.

46
00:03:44,190 --> 00:03:48,540
As the city's protector, she protected it from foreign enemies, exercising as a warrior goddess,

47
00:03:48,540 --> 00:03:53,630
but in a different way than Ares'. She did not even have weapons, she took them to borrow from Zeus,

48
00:03:53,630 --> 00:03:59,209
and she never sacrificed uselessly her soldiers. She didn't love war

49
00:03:59,209 --> 00:04:04,680
and she only supported the more favorable battles.

50
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:08,940
She also was a great advisor for a lot of classic heroes. She taught Heracles

51
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:13,910
how to flay the Nemea's lion using its own claws to cut its thick skin.

52
00:04:13,910 --> 00:04:18,030
She also helped him to kill the Lerna's hydra.

53
00:04:18,030 --> 00:04:22,290
During the Trojan War she was with greeks, and after the battle helped Ulysses

54
00:04:22,290 --> 00:04:28,490
telling him what he had to do to recover his wife Penelope and his kingdom. In the fable

55
00:04:28,490 --> 00:04:34,520
of Jason and the Argonauts, she's the one who teaches to the builders of the ship "Argo".

56
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:39,770
Today, Athena still has a big relevance. Her statue appears in a lot of government buildings

57
00:04:39,770 --> 00:04:44,210
of America and Europe, like the Vienna Parliament. And also in so many coins,

58
00:04:44,210 --> 00:04:48,840
like the American one of 50 dollars of 1915,

59
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:52,400
the most valuable one of its history.

60
00:04:52,400 --> 00:04:56,300
Athena has so many myths and stories that we could be hours talking about her.

61
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:59,520
But we would like to talk about so many other gods, tiktakers.

62
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:02,440
Ask us for your favorite ones at the comments!